    "_smooth_window_doc": "2026-10-29 (ledger 0060): osm_fixes.json is a list of 79 OSM nodes (18 m apart on the corners, up to 585 m on the straights), not a 1 Hz GPS drive; from_track's 5-fix moving average cut its corners by up to 26.8 m and parted the closed ring's ends by 466 m (bridged with a chord): the deck floated over ground the track is not on and the engine minted four bridges. 0 = no smoothing.",
    "_note": "RE-SOURCED 2026-07-25 from the REAL High Plains Raceway at 93301 E US Hwy 36, Deer Trail CO (39.7353,-103.8980). Replaces fabricated compressed lat/lon traced off the old unified map (which placed it at 39.67,-104.77, ~70 km away). Geometry is the closed cycle of OSM highway=raceway ways: Short North, Bikers Berm, Niagara, Dannys Lesson, High Plains Drifter, Prarie Corkscrew, Full West + one unnamed link = 3220 m (2.00 mi). The north section (To Hell On A Bobsled / Ladder To Heaven) is EXCLUDED: its south end is unmapped in OSM, leaving a 110 m gap that would have to be invented to close the full 2.55-mile course (LAWS L1 — never invent geometry). Add it by tracing that 110 m off a georeferenced aerial, then re-chain. Pit Lane excluded (not the racing line). Winding CW to match the other CO circuits. Elevation from USGS 3DEP at the real site.",
    "_width_note": "default_width_m 12.0 is INHERITED FROM THE FABRICATED CONFIG and unverified against the real circuit."
